    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0260" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg890"/>

                <head>No. 391.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Sickles.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 14,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I understand from your telegrams of 12th and 13th that you have recognized the
                    new government. It will be grateful to know that you have regarded the condition
                    and prospects of the republic such as to justify the discretionary power given
                    you in that regard. This Government and people look with sincere and earnest
                    hope for the peaceful and permanent establishment of the new government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
